   "rect": [
    243.7,
    599.7,
    485.6,
    714.3
   ],
   "value": "Intent, objective, and functional statements are part of the objective-based format of the National Model Codes. Objectives define the overall goals of the Code (e.g., safety, health, fire protection), while functional statements describe the required performance or role of building elements to achieve those objectives. Intent statements provide explanatory guidance on the reasoning behind specific Code provisions and how they contribute to achieving the associated objectives and functional statements. These resources can be found in Division A of the applicable Code or in the National Research Council (NRC) Intent Statements Supplement available online.",
   "on_state": null,
